      "text": "Laguna Niguel's name blends Spanish \"laguna\" for lagoon with Acjachemem village \"Niguili\" near Aliso Creek.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laguna_Niguel%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "First recorded residents were the Acjachemem Native Americans, who may have had a village called \"Niguili\" near Aliso Creek.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laguna_Niguel%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1959, the Laguna Niguel Corporation bought Rancho Niguel land to create one of California's first master‑planned communities.",
